WEBVTT

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.880
A young man traveled across the ocean to study music.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:11.620
In a far off country, he met a very small and extraordinary creature.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.920
The tiny creature was injured, so feeling pity for it, he treated it.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.080
Upon doing so...

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.340
I owe you my life.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:28.110
For this, I will grant the blessing of music to the school you build.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.620
Now, some time has passed.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.130
Another extraordinary encounter has taken place.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.710
Hihara-kun?

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.630
Hino-chan should be performing soon.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.360
I wonder if she'll be all right.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.560
Hihara-kun.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:49.610
What's wrong?

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.870
Oh, no! It's nothing!

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.160
Do your best, Hino-chan!

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.130
The Anonymous Chopin

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.720
How far did I play?

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.850
What should I do?

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.100
I'm screwed!

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.960
It's different from just with the violin

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.880
and also just with the trumpet.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.490
When you combine the two,

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.200
it becomes even more pleasurable.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.130
Thank you! Thank you!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.720
You're too kind! Thanks!

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.840
I actually... played it?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.820
Wow! That's great, great!

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:09.380
It's interesting to hear the violin and trumpet together, huh?

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.310
I love cute performances like that.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.590
We don't approve of this!

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:17.300
It's cowardly to play with accompaniment!

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:18.370
Yeah!

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.170
Hold on! It's not her fault.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:24.250
I butted in without asking her.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.240
Sorry.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:31.210
Besides, didn't Yunoki say to help her out?

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:36.160
How saddening... My feelings didn't get through to them.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.660
W-We know!

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.210
Do excuse us!

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.330
Huh? Was it something I said?

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.640
Kaho-chan!

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.510
You were great!

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:52.130
You're incredible, Kaho!

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:53.540
Thank you.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:54.460
Hino-chan!

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.560
Y-Yes?

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.640
That was fun. Let's play together again!

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.200
Sure!

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:10.160
Making noise and making music are two different things.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.430
I feel like I'm beginning to understand that.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:18.630
I had no idea Kaho-chan was so good at playing the violin!

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.500
That must be why you were picked for the competition.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.050
We'll support you, so do your best, OK?

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.610
S-Sure.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:26.770
Thank you.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:34.350
Faculty Room

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.350
You aren't sure what to do exactly?

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.620
Yes.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.310
Don't ask me.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:41.190
But, Sensei, aren't you in charge of the competition?

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:46.280
Yes, in name only. In charge in name only.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:51.500
Oh, right. I suppose you can start by choosing which piece to perform

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.300
after the first selection's theme is announced.

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:57.550
Also, you can talk to the other people in the competition.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:58.540
The others?

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:04.270
You know... How they practice and what sort of study materials they use.

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:06.410
Why not ask Tsukimori?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.670
Tsukimori-kun?

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:10.720
You're interfering with my practice.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.800
I couldn't! I really couldn't!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.390
Have you found an accompanist yet?

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.030
Accompanist?

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:22.730
I know I explained this to you. You need a piano accompanist in the competition.

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:24.550
What?

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.020
Want to go get crepes today?

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:29.700
Sure.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:34.490
Asking Hihara-sempai would be much easier, but he plays a different instrument...

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:38.660
Well, we're both second years, so I shouldn't be so scared.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.420
What?! Say that again, Tsukimori!

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.670
Tsukimori-kun?

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:48.720
Sempais, if you want to enter the competition that badly,

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:52.260
shouldn't you be complaining to the school instead of me?

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:57.100
Even if I were to withdraw, I don't think you two would be chosen.

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.080
He's adding fuel to the fire!

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.270
Why you!

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:04.820
Keep your mouth shut!

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.950
What the hell was that for?

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.070
Umm... Girls against violence?

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:22.200
Are you screwing around?!

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.170
Ow...

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:35.810
Now I've done it...

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.680
Let me see.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:41.350
She fell all by herself!

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:44.200
I-I'm fine, Tsukimori-kun.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.780
It's gonna get all bloody.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.870
Seriously, I'm fine.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.660
You play the violin with those fingers, do you not?

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:02.790
School Infirmary

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:04.700
Thank you.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.920
And sorry for getting you wet.

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.200
You're really a handful, you know that?

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.990
And you even hurt yourself.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.960
You know a cut like that will affect your performance.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:19.760
What?

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.830
You're really incredible.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:25.230
You practice everyday, you take care of your body...

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:28.610
Your life revolves around the violin, doesn't it?

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.330
Yeah, so?

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:34.860
Right. I just figure you must really love the violin.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:36.560
That's stupid.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:37.400
Huh?

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:43.290
Whether you love it or hate is is completely pointless.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.370
Then why do you play the violin?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.880
That's none of your business.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.460
Tsukimori-kun...

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.710
I wonder if I hit a sore spot.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:05.590
You play the violin with those fingers, do you not?

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.360
Oh, Shimizu. Glad I ran into you.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:21.120
What is it, Kaneda-sensei?

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.400
It's Kanazawa.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:23.830
Excuse me.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.230
Oh, perfect timing.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.280
Tsukimori!

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.010
Huh?

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:32.130
Kaho, your shooting is terrible.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:36.130
Really? I thought my form was getting pretty good.

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:38.270
Ow!

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.710
Man...

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:41.970
I'm sorry!

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.020
Hino?

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.760
Tsuchiura-kun!

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.960
What do you think you're doing?

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:48.970
Sorry, sorry.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:51.280
We were playing soccer in gym today.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.720
Oh? That must have been tough.

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:57.310
Oh, but I made a great shot.

00:09:57.310 --> 00:10:00.170
Oh? How's it compare to this one?

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:02.830
That was a bit of a miss...

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.450
Kaho, you know,

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.120
if you were being tested on soccer this year, you'd have failed.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.740
Leave me alone.

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:10.690
Hino-san.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:12.960
Tsukimori-kun?

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:16.760
Kanazawa-sensei asked me to give you this.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.470
Oh? You came here just for me?

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:24.910
Hino got hurt when she stuck up for you?

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:26.750
Then, if you think about it,

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:30.300
there's no reason you can't take this to her.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:35.800
Hey, why did you have to sigh just there?

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.650
And... what's this?

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.520
School-wide Competition First Selection?

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:45.810
What?! It's starting already? It hasn't even been two weeks!

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:46.990
I guess so.

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:49.720
What piece will you be playing, Tsukimori-kun?

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:50.740
Me?

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:54.840
I mean... How do you practice, normally?

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.590
And how do you pick up the songs you choose?

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.420
I have lots to ask you...

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.740
I have no obligation to tell you those things.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:04.010
Besides, I doubt it'd help any, if I did.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:10.880
Anyway, take care to not let the quality of your performance in the competition drop any, OK?

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:13.940
The quality of her performance, huh?

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:20.020
Mr. Music Department here must be quite confident in his skills, huh?

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.100
So what?

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:27.190
I just want to compete at a high level to win the competition.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.080
That's stupid.

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.660
Stupid?

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:34.360
H-Hey... What's going on between these two?

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:54.230
Stupid? Us in the Music Department work hard at our performance every day.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:57.190
Are you saying people in General Studies don't?

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:02.050
It's a matter of attitude towards music.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:05.060
You have no legs to stand on here.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:06.630
Excuse me.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.380
It can't be helped, since you're in General Studies,

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.620
but take care of your fingers during gym.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:24.420
Geez... What's with the pretentious attitude?

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:28.550
No legs to stand on, huh?

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:29.610
Is something the matter?

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.760
Ah... No, it's fine.

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:38.390
Anyway, I'll be going.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.520
Hey, Tsuchiura. Practice is cancelled today.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:53.490
Hey, that was Tsuchiura-kun from the soccer team, right?

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:56.680
When did you two get so close?

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:57.420
Huh?

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.280
Lucky girl!

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:00.290
Huh?

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:01.950
Hino-chan!

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.030
Hihara-sempai!

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.490
Heading home?

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:10.060
Yes. How about you?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.390
Me? I've got practice today.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.290
They decided on the first selection.

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:18.320
I don't really like to practice, but I want to give a good performance!

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:23.640
Let's do our best!

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:30.730
Hey, isn't that the guy who saved you the other day?

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:33.610
He looks so cheerful and kind.

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:37.120
Tsukimori is so cool and good-looking,

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:40.550
and Yunoki-san is a wonderful man as well!

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:44.590
Kaho-chan, it looks like that Violin Romance is coming true!

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:44.590
A Girl's Youthful Delusions

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:48.300
I don't have time for romance.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:54.850
Oh, long time no see.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:56.870
What brings about this visit?

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:01.900
You haven't come by for a while.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:05.640
This guy here hasn't had any company and has been pretty lonely.

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:09.860
Oh, yeah. Would you play a few bars?

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:13.580
I'd love to hear you play the piano again.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.630
I'll go listen to some tracks off of this CD I bought.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:36.550
Huh? I think I heard something just now...

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.530
Minami Instruments

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:58.700
I didn't know there was a music shop here.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:16.750
Amazing... The sound is so rich.

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:42.540
Tsuchiura-kun? Why?

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.420
But... his piano-playing is amazing...

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:55.320
It's Chopin's "Fantasia".

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:58.630
This piece requires quite a range to play.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:05.480
Hino! What are you doing here?

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:08.600
Uh, I was just walking by, and...

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.650
I never imagined that you can play the piano...

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:20.660
Don't say a word of this to anyone!

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.540
What's the matter, Hihara?

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.600
I'm worn out from practicing.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.350
What are you talking about?

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:39.470
They chose the selection earlier than I thought they would.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:45.310
That's true. Plus you have to choose your song based on the theme they announced.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:46.860
Oh yeah! The theme!

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:49.990
The first selection's theme is...

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:51.500
"A Beginning".

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:54.030
Minami Instruments

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.610
Don't say a word of this to anyone!

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:59.280
Do you mean about you playing the... piano?

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.320
Why not?

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.160
Please.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:10.400
Now, now. Calm down, Ryo.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:18.190
You must be a student at Seiso, huh?

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:20.010
Are you looking for something?

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.520
Oh, no, it's not...

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:27.270
What, Hino? You came here for no reason at all?

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:31.540
Should you be slacking off like this with the competition approaching?

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:32.980
Oh, no, umm...

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.500
Competition?

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:38.530
Oh, I see. A school-wide competition.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:41.430
It's wonderful that you were chosen.

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:43.760
Oh, no. I'm a complete amateur.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:46.710
I don't even know the basics.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.400
What about the theme?

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:53.220
Yeah, and an accompanist... I have lots I have to decide upon.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:57.040
Then why not have Ryo do it?

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:02.890
Don't even joke like that!

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.150
What?

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.600
Don't "what" me!

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:08.990
Well, you are so talented...

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:12.220
I feel like your talents would be wasted if you were my accompanist.

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:14.680
That's not what I meant.

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:19.150
Well, well. This must be fate!

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:23.620
Putting accompaniment aside, is there anything else he can help you with?

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.620
No, it's really OK...

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:30.720
It's fine! Besides, Ryo is experienced when it comes to competitions.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:31.980
Huh?

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:35.830
His mother is a piano teacher. He's quite knowledgeable.

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.190
Really?

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.130
That's amazing, Tsuchiura-kun.

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:45.600
Those days are long gone.

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:51.090
Sorry.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.640
It's fine. Your secret's safe with me.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.030
I'm going home.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.110
Huh?

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.600
See you, Hino. Later.

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.080
Uh, OK...

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.850
I wonder if I made him feel bad.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:15.850
And he's been helping me out so much lately, too...

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:22.010
I think Ryo's worried about you.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:23.190
What?

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:27.830
BA-DUMP!

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:27.030
Because you're a General Studies student like him, and yet you'll be in the competition.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.020
Oh, that's what you meant.

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:32.760
It's been ages since he played the piano in here.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:35.020
I wonder if something happened at school.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.910
Could it be...

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:41.050
You have no legs to stand on here.

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:44.870
Minami Instruments

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:50.100
Tsuchiura-kun used to come here a lot, huh?

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.830
Ah, indeed.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:54.840
Since he was the same height as that piano.

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:59.430
He used to come and play on his way home from school.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:04.400
Has he since quit playing?

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:08.010
He may be happier if he did quit.

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:15.960
I have to decide on a song to play,

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:17.910
and I need to find an accompanist.

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:19.070
Hino-chan!

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:20.970
What am I going to do?

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:22.290
Hino-chan!

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.580
Good morning!

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:28.090
Good morning.

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:29.850
Good morning, Hino-san.

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:32.720
You were spacing out there. Something on your mind?

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:35.540
Yeah... It's about the competition...

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:39.420
I don't know anyone who can be my accompanist.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:43.860
That's true. Must be hard for a General Studies student to find one.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:45.890
I can introduce you to one, if you'd like.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:47.840
Can you really?!

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:53.230
There are plenty of girls who volunteered to play for me.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:55.330
I'm sure one of them could...

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.100
Would that mean...

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:04.510
I-I'm sorry! I truly appreciate the offer, Yunoki-sempai,

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:06.220
but I'll manage on my own somehow!

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.020
Are you sure?

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:13.800
Later, Hino-chan!

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:15.170
Goodbye.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:17.820
Hino-sempai!

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:18.630
Huh?

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:24.110
How do you do? I'm a first year Music student, Megumi Shoji.

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:25.630
Oh, hello.

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:31.600
Umm, if you haven't chosen an accompanist yet, would you please pick me?

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.140
What? Really?

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:38.220
Yes. I want to participate in the competition in one form or another.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.480
I'd like that!

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:46.070
Me too! I look forward to playing with you!

00:21:53.970 --> 00:21:57.000
This is great. I found an accompanist.

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:39.720
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:39.710
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:42.840
The trumpet is played by pressing the valves with your right hand

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:47.000
while you blow in and adjust the length of the tube with your left hand.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:50.170
Because the sound reverberates quite loudly, it's often used in public shows.

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:55.670
Long ago, various kings in Europe competed to see how many trumpeters they could employ.

00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:57.870
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:57.870 --> 00:24:01.130
The trumpet and the five yen coin have something in common.

00:24:01.130 --> 00:24:02.940
What could it be?

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:05.150
The answer is at the end of this program!

00:24:05.150 --> 00:24:09.130
Next Episode

00:24:05.900 --> 00:24:07.600
Special news!

00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:10.730
There's a top-secret shocking video of Tsuchiura-kun!

00:24:10.730 --> 00:24:12.450
Hey! Don't watch!

00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:15.850
Hey, could you not say "Don't watch" during the next episode preview?

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:18.300
Next episode: The Waltz of the Bewildered Heart.

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:19.470
Please watch.

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:21.670
The answer is...

00:24:22.330 --> 00:24:24.610
They're both made of brass!
